            "speaker": "B",
            "hanzi": "好，到了以后给我打电话。",
            "pinyin": "Hǎo, dào le yǐhòu gěi wǒ dǎ diànhuà.",
            "english": "Okay, call me after you arrive."
          }
        ]
      },
      "patterns": [
        {
          "id": "pattern-1",
          "title": "Movement from the speaker’s viewpoint",
          "explanation_en": "来 (lái) means motion toward a reference point; 去 (qù) means away. 回 (huí) conveys returning.",
          "formula_en": "subject + 来/去/回 + place",
          "examples": [
            {
              "hanzi": "朋友明天来我家。",
              "pinyin": "Péngyou míngtiān lái wǒ jiā.",
              "english": "A friend is coming to my home tomorrow."
            },
            {
              "hanzi": "我下午回家。",
              "pinyin": "Wǒ xiàwǔ huí jiā.",
              "english": "I will go home this afternoon."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "pattern-2",
          "title": "Places and destinations",
          "explanation_en": "到 (dào) marks arrival at a destination. In the simplest travel patterns, use 坐 (zuò) for taking transport such as a taxi or train.",
          "formula_en": "坐 + vehicle + 去 + place",
          "examples": [
            {
              "hanzi": "我们坐火车去北京。",
              "pinyin": "Wǒmen zuò huǒchē qù Běijīng.",
              "english": "We are taking the train to Beijing."
            },
            {
              "hanzi": "他晚上到学校。",
              "pinyin": "Tā wǎnshang dào xuéxiào.",
              "english": "He will arrive at school in the evening."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
